# The states of a diagram cell

A cell's bar names its state: **drawn**, **stale**, or **not drawn**. Back to
[[index]].

## A cell that draws

```mermaid#show
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> NotDrawn
  NotDrawn --> Drawn: the source draws
  Drawn --> Stale: an edit that does not draw
  Stale --> Drawn: the source draws again
  Drawn --> Drawn: an edit that draws
```

To see **stale**, break the cell above while the preview is open: delete the
`>` of one arrow. The drawing stays, dimmed, with the renderer's message under
it. Put the character back and the cell is drawn again.

## A cell that never drew

This source has a syntax error, so there is no drawing to keep. The cell shows
its source and the reason.

```mermaid#show
flowchart TD
  A --> --> [
```

## A cell in D2 that never drew

```d2#show
a -> {
```

## Configuration inside the fence

A diagram can configure itself. This one asks for Mermaid's dark theme.

```mermaid#show
%%{init: {"theme": "dark"}}%%
flowchart LR
  light --> dark
```
